                  %mi T
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash t \Vdash T \qquad
            (element in a type) (realizer of a type)
          %p
            Note that in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nuprl"} Nuprl
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi t
                    %mo ⊩
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash t \Vdash T
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⌊
                    %mi ext
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⌋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash T\;\lfloor ext t \rfloor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+type"} inhabited
          %p In the rules below, however, no attention is paid to what can be metatheoretically computed with terms or derivations. That is (important) future work.
          %p
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi t
                  %mo ⊩
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash t \Vdash T
            ) is used instead of (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi t
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash t\,:\,T
            ) in order to avoid the misinterpretation of this judgment form as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intrinsic+and+extrinsic+views+of+typing"} intrinsic typing
            of terms. Note the contrast with variables, which
            %em are
            intrinsically typed.
          %p
            The (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\,:\,T
            ) form can be translated to this system as either (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ⊩
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \Vdash T
            ) or (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ?
                  %mo ⊩
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ? \Vdash t \in T
            ). The latter uses the abbreviation “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in
            ” defined below, and the abuse of meta-notation that we don’t care what goes in the “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ?
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ?
            ”. With (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ⊩
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \Vdash T
            ), we think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            as resulting from the proof of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ?
                    %mo ⊩
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ? \Vdash t \in T
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %em semantic judgment
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in T
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo ?
                    %mo ⊩
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash ? \Vdash T
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash T
          %h3#abbreviations Abbreviations
          %h4#SemJudg Semantic Judgment Forms
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A\;\coloneqq\;a = a \in A
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Π
                  %munder
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo .
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B\;\coloneqq\;\Pi \underline{\;}:A.B
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %munder
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \wedge B\;\coloneqq\;\{\underline{\;}:A | B\}
          %p
            “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            equality is respected in
            = succeed ".\u201D:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Π
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mi Comp
                  %mo .
                  %mi Π
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %mi Comp
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \prec B\;\coloneqq\;\Pi t:Comp.\Pi t':Comp.
                  (t \in B)\to(t = t' \in A)\to(t = t' \in B)
          %p
            “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            members are included in
            = succeed ".\u201D:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Π
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mi Comp
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq B\;\coloneqq\;\Pi t:Comp.(t \in A)\to(t \in B)
          %p
            “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a subtype of
            = succeed ".\u201D:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi λ
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \lt\!\!:\;B\;\coloneqq\;(\lambda x.x) \in (A \to B)
          %p
            Note: (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \lt\!\!:\;B
            ) ought to be logically equivalent to (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq B \wedge A \prec B
            ), using the rules. And also to (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mi Comp
                  %mo .
                  %mi Π
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %mi Comp
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi t:Comp.\Pi t':Comp.(t = t' \in A)\to(t = t' \in B)
            ). So thinking of types as PERs, subtypes are subrelations.
          %p
            “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a refinement/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subquotient"} subquotient
            of
            = succeed ".\u201D:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊑
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \sqsubseteq B\;\coloneqq\;A \subseteq B \wedge B \prec A
          %p
            Note the reversal of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≺
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prec
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
