          %h3#miscellaneous Miscellaneous
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⊩
                      %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{x:T \in \Gamma}{\Gamma \vdash x \Vdash T}
          %p The untyped beta conversion rules have the same role as Nuprl’s direct computation rules:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "true", :rowspacing => "1.0ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi A
                              %msub
                                %mo ≡
                                %mi β
                              %mi B
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi B
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi type
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi t
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi t
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi t
                              %msub
                                %mo ≡
                                %mi β
                              %mi t
                              %mo ′
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi t
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi T
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi t
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{gathered}
                  \\frac{A \equiv_\beta B \qquad \Gamma \vdash B\,type \qquad
                  \\Gamma \vdash t \Vdash A}
                  {\Gamma \vdash t \Vdash B} \\
                  \\\
                  \\frac{t \equiv_\beta t' \qquad \Gamma \vdash t \Vdash T}
                  {\Gamma \vdash t' \Vdash T}
                  \\end{gathered}
          %p
            Every type respects itself, and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Comp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "true", :rowspacing => "1.0ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi A
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi type
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi p
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi A
                              %mo ≺
                              %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi A
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi type
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi p
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi Comp
                              %mo ≺
                              %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{gathered}
                  \\frac{\Gamma \vdash A\,type}{\Gamma \vdash p \Vdash A \prec A} \\
                  \\\
                  \\frac{\Gamma \vdash A\,type}{\Gamma \vdash p \Vdash Comp \prec A}
                  \\end{gathered}
          %h3#equality Equality
          %p A reflexivity rule, but any term can be the proof:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi t
                      %mo ⊩
                      %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo ⊩
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash t \Vdash T}{\Gamma \vdash p \Vdash t = t \in T}
          %p Terms participating in equality are elements. Normally this would only be admissible, but in CLF, it comes in handy to make it into “selectivity” rules:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "true", :rowspacing => "1.0ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi p
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi t
                              %mn 1
                              %mo =
                              %mi t
                              %mn 2
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi T
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi t
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi T
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi p
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi t
                              %mn 1
                              %mo =
                              %mi t
                              %mn 2
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi T
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi t
                              %mn 2
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{gathered}
                  \\frac{\Gamma \vdash p \Vdash t1 = t2 \in T}{\Gamma \vdash t1 \Vdash T} \\
                  \\\
                  \\frac{\Gamma \vdash p \Vdash t1 = t2 \in T}{\Gamma \vdash t2 \Vdash T}
                  \\end{gathered}
          %p
            Note that the above equality rules make (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi t
                  %mo ⊩
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash t \Vdash T
            ) and (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash t \in T
            ) interderivable, as promised.
          %p
            We use a “subsumptive” rewrite rule as equality elimination. “Subsumptive” refers to the property that the realizer of the type we rewrite in is unaffected. The terminology “subsumptive” for this is new to CLF, although this is effectively the same equality elimination rule as in Nuprl. The terminology comes from “subsumptive” vs “coercive” implementations of subtyping. Note that formally, CLF has no typed judgmental equality. Semantically, it’s an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional type theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi type
                      %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo ⊩
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo ⊩
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo ⊩
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{\Gamma,x:A \vdash B\,type \qquad
                  \\Gamma \vdash p \Vdash a1 = a2 \in A \qquad
                  \\Gamma \vdash b \Vdash B[a1/x]}
                  {\Gamma \vdash b \Vdash B[a2/x]}
          %p Any two terms are equal as the (consequently unique) proof of a true equality:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi t
                      %mo ⊩
                      %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi q
                      %mo ⊩
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{\Gamma \vdash t \Vdash T}
                  {\Gamma \vdash q \Vdash p1 = p2 \in (t = t \in T)}
          %p
            That means
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top
            too, which is thus the maximum PER, ordered by subtyping. (Well, just as soon as we make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tru
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tru
            an element of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
          %h3#functions Functions
          %p We have the standard application rule, and a variant of function extensionality:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "true", :rowspacing => "1.0ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi f
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi Π
                              %mi x
                              %mo :
                              %mi A
                              %mo .
                              %mi B
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi a
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi f
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi a
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi A
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi type
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ,
                              %mi x
                              %mo :
                              %mi A
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi p
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi f
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo =
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi B
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∉
                              %mi FV
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %mo ,
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi q
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mi f
                              %mo =
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Π
                              %mi x
                              %mo :
                              %mi A
                              %mo .
                              %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{gathered}
                  \\frac{\Gamma \vdash f \Vdash \Pi x:A.B \qquad
                  \\Gamma \vdash a \Vdash A}
                  {\Gamma \vdash f\,a \Vdash B[a/x]} \\
                  \\\
                  \\frac{\Gamma \vdash A\,type \qquad
                  \\Gamma,x:A \vdash p \Vdash f\,x = f'\,x \in B \qquad
                  x \notin FV(f,f')}
                  {\Gamma \vdash q \Vdash f = f' \in \Pi x:A.B}
                  \\end{gathered}
          %p
            Unconventionally, we consider function extensionality to be the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            intro rule, and derive the fact that lambdas implement functions.
          %h3#intersection Intersection
          %p
            Elements of a family intersection are like elements of a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            type, except you don’t have to apply them. An intersection element is
            %em already
            an element of all instances of the family. So the rules for family intersection are analogous to the rules for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "true", :rowspacing => "1.0ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mi b
                              %mo ⊩
                              %mo ∩
                              %mi x
                              %mo :
                              %mi A
                              %mo .
