          %h3#subset Subset
          %p The subset type resembles an existential quantifier. In the elimination rule, the proof part must be computationally irrelevant, since an element of a subset does not include the proof. Nuprl handles this with a hidden assumption, which is the practical way to do it. But it’s also sound to just stick in a free variable side condition.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
